<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37817" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαγγ-ελία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>command, summons,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				9.38.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>announcement, notice,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				22.1235.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἀγῶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					561.9
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Chalcis</span>), prob. in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ma.</u>
				10.15
			</span></i>; v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Jo.</u>
				1.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as law-term,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοκιμασίας</span>) <i>summons to attend</i> a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοκιμασία τῶν ῥητόρων</span> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαγγέλλω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3
				</span></i>
			), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὶ ἐπαγγέλλειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					1.64
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				81
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τοὺς θεσμοθέτας ἔσθ᾽ ἡμῖν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					22.29
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>notification, summons,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sammelb.
				4434
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>offer, promise, profession, undertaking,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ὑπερβολὰς τῶν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1164a29
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1251.20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαγγελίας ποιεῖσθαί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.72.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἐν ἐπαγγελίᾳ
			καταλιπών</span> having left it as <i>a promise,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				18.28.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἐ. ἐπὶ τέλος
			ἀγαγεῖν</span> ibid., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				577.11
			</span></i> (Milet., <span class="entity">iii/ii B. C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤμων ἐπαγγελίᾳ</span>
			<i>the promise</i> of his shoulders, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἐ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαγγειλάμενος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				11.12
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Lagina</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιησάμενος ἐκ τῶν ἰδίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Michel</u>
					473.10
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Mylasa</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐβεβαίωσεν τὴν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Inscr.Prien.</u>
					123.9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				3624a34
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>indication,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἐσομένου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					205.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> pl.,
				<i>canvassing,</i>
			= Lat. <i>ambitus,</i> prob. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ-</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.276d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπάγγελμα</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, <i>subject</i> of a treatise, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Libr.Propr.Prooem.</u>
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>7.</b> the <i>curative property
				claimed</i> for prescriptions or drugs, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς τῶν φαρμάκων ἐ.</span> their <i>advertised
				properties,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.5.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.504
			</span></i>,al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐπιτηδεύματος</span>
			<i>public exercise</i> of a profession, Men.Prot.<i><span class="en">
				p.1D.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
